   "synthesis": "- Highest-value pattern = **source → pollutant → transformation → effect**, not isolated definitions.\n- UPSC repeatedly tests unfamiliar chemicals through **product association + persistence + trophic/health pathway**.\n- Elimination hinges on qualifiers: **primary vs secondary; gas vs particulate; PM₁₀ vs PM₂.₅; GHG vs air pollutant; persistent vs biodegradable; source-specific vs universal**.\n- Industrial pollution is recurrent enough to retain a compact **industry-emission matrix** rather than memorising one-off factories.\n- UPPCS adds simple named-recall anchors; keep them in a separate extension layer so they do not inflate UPSC notes."
